From 6b85f8e688f79642c270f47a18d62f145304d1bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Storey <martinstorey@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:07:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] agent access on macos 27: say the files & folders switch,
 not a dialog (claude, node .mcpb)

macOS 27 denies an agent app's first read of our container with no prompt;
the grant is System Settings > Privacy & Security > Files & Folders >
(app) > Bristlenose. Measured for Claude and ChatGPT, 29 Sep 2026
(docs/design-mcp-files-and-folders.md section 1).

- proxy: the permission sentence branches on macOS 27 and names the host the
  package declares (BRISTLENOSE_MCP_HOST; fallback "your AI app"); the
  macOS 26 dialog sentence keeps the host too. Dev-only override for tests,
  stripped at pack time; check-mcpb now rejects any BRISTLENOSE_DEV_* in a pack.
- .mcpb manifest declares BRISTLENOSE_MCP_HOST=Claude.
- Settings > MCP Agents, Claude tab: on 27 the note names the switch, with an
  Open Files & Folders button (deep link, falls back to System Settings).
  macOS 26 keeps the existing dialog note.
- two keys x 21 locales, pane names lifted from macOS 27's own loctables.
- tests/test_mcpb_proxy_messages.py drives the real proxy under node;
  proven red on the unpatched proxy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
